ms for Record Robustness"}, {"id": "scrambling-records-01", "next_step": "Synthesize literature on OTOCs versus environmental decoherence indicators.", "question": "Can quantum scrambling and the formation of redundant, objective records be distinguished via measurable criteria in complex many-body systems?", "title": "Divergence of Scrambling and Redundancy"}], "beliefs": [], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "nb-objective-records-01", "project": "objective-records-01", "provenance": ["source-f444a12ad77a4bc7", "peer-23d4431c2f184f300bef23ea", "peer-3d80ce4af7c184d54bcc9333", "peer-69bb733fb4e0a3d67ac10066"], "revision": 6, "summary": "Objective physical records emerge through the redundant broadcast of pointer states into the environment, a process that enables multiple independent observers to access consistent information without disturbing the source system. This objective character is grounded in the stability of pointer states under decoherenc…", "title": "Operational Frameworks for Objective Records"}, {"id": "nb-record-robustness-01", "project": "record-robustness-01", "provenance": ["peer-3d80ce4af7c184d54bcc9333", "peer-feb7891b837e677ec8e3c811", "source-0af46fdac3ca4296"], "revision": 10, "summary": "Robustness in physical records is achieved when system pointer states are redundantly encoded into environmental degrees of freedom, enabling independent observers to reach consensus. This process, formalizable through Spectrum Broadcast Structures (SBS) and quantum Darwinism, effectively 'broadcasts' information. Fur…", "title": "Robustness and Redundancy in Quantum and Classical Records"}, {"id": "nb-scrambling-records-01", "project": "scrambling-records-01", "provenance": ["peer-d5a5b609385e5c5c27ca4c79", "source-fa07ca798c9847a9"], "revision": 1, "summary": "Quantum scrambling, characterized by rapid information delocalization, often competes with the formation of redundant records. While scrambling tends to erase local information, the subsequent emergence of objective records suggests a complex trade-off between information spreading and environmental encoding.", "title": "Divergence of Scrambling and Redundancy"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "42f19fe358217ebdc87ce6b1aeb008848ae5dfc66d5583ce540a4e12563039ec", "hash": "ad3943e9391d46a9843fa30dc970e4aae6d7ec24d08d4b9b9f7c2843fae23d7e"}, {"seq": 3607, "time": "2026-10-17T15:32:44.062267+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 47421, "provider_input_hash": "1d545b1084291b0fe1654df465691f09393adffdb61499f9dc11d651f2a70f39", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "w-c85da88f5e014a25"}, "prev_hash": "ad3943e9391d46a9843fa30dc970e4aae6d7ec24d08d4b9b9f7c2843fae23d7e", "hash": "092e6189bcd318905de416f4d2e7cfd8a5ebc6a53e7e6ff06ab27765990a586e"}, {"seq": 3608, "time": "2026-10-17T15:33:43.834715+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_finished", "payload": {"attempt": {"elapsed_ms": 20247, "finish_reason": "STOP", "http_status": 200, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "model_version": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider": "google-gemini", "provider_input_chars": 47421, "provider_input_hash": "1d545b1084291b0fe1654df465691f09393adffdb61499f9dc11d651f2a70f39", "request_payload_bytes": 51443, "result": "success", "usage": {"candidatesTokenCount": 1711, "promptTokenCount": 14174, "promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT", "tokenCount": 14174}], "serviceTier": "standard", "thoughtsTokenCount": 932, "totalTokenCount": 16817}, "web_evidence": {"search_queries": [], "sources": [], "url_retrievals": []}}, "id": "w-c85da88f5e014a25"}, "prev_has